00:58:23.700 --> 00:58:24.260
Wow.

1373
00:58:24.560 --> 00:58:24.840
Yeah.

1374
00:58:25.160 --> 00:58:26.200
What was number two?

1375
00:58:27.000 --> 00:58:27.560
Rabbit.

1376
00:58:28.580 --> 00:58:29.140
Rabbit.

1377
00:58:29.520 --> 00:58:29.820
Mm-hmm.

1378
00:58:30.280 --> 00:58:32.740
That one came out of left field for me.

1379
00:58:32.920 --> 00:58:33.320
I know.

1380
00:58:33.580 --> 00:58:35.800
More Halloween festivities are happening now.

1381
00:58:36.160 --> 00:58:40.300
A few folks are playing with the Ouija board by front reception, and Michael's determined

1382
00:58:40.300 --> 00:58:42.880
to make a ghost call Daryl an ass.

1383
00:58:43.140 --> 00:58:43.580
Mm-hmm.

1384
00:58:44.120 --> 00:58:47.260
And then in the conference room, folks are bobbing for apples.

1385
00:58:47.560 --> 00:58:49.940
We have a fan catch from Emily H.

1386
00:58:50.260 --> 00:58:53.160
in Tennessee that is so amazing.

1387
00:58:53.880 --> 00:58:56.260
It's about this apple bobbing scene.

1388
00:58:56.540 --> 00:58:56.900
Okay.

1389
00:58:57.420 --> 00:58:58.500
Emily said,

1390
00:58:58.500 --> 00:59:03.700
I thought my eyes were playing tricks on me, but I'm not making this up, in all caps.

1391
00:59:04.100 --> 00:59:07.580
All throughout this episode, Meredith is wearing a blonde wig.

1392
00:59:08.320 --> 00:59:13.560
But in the opening credits, starting with Goodbye Michael, I believe, the scene in which

1393
00:59:13.560 --> 00:59:18.220
Erin is bobbing for apples is used, and it shows Meredith in a red wig.

1394
00:59:18.600 --> 00:59:19.100
Oh.

1395
00:59:19.460 --> 00:59:23.880
I had to go back to this episode, and sure enough, her wig is blonde.

1396
00:59:24.320 --> 00:59:26.020
Why did they do that?

1397
00:59:26.020 --> 00:59:31.120
I am sure many people have written in about this, but I just never noticed it until now.

1398
00:59:31.500 --> 00:59:32.860
So here's what I did.

1399
00:59:33.000 --> 00:59:38.100
These extended credits of Erin bobbing for apples, they've actually been playing since

1400
00:59:38.100 --> 00:59:39.380
the beginning of this season.

1401
00:59:39.680 --> 00:59:46.560
So the first thing I did was go back and look at the opening credits, and I even took

1402
00:59:46.560 --> 00:59:47.200
a screenshot.

1403
00:59:47.560 --> 00:59:53.300
The extended credits are in Andy's play, and Meredith is wearing the blonde wig.

1404
00:59:53.300 --> 00:59:53.800
Mm-hmm.

1405
00:59:54.500 --> 00:59:56.200
Just like in this episode.

1406
00:59:56.440 --> 00:59:59.520
And I thought, oh, well, maybe Emily is just mistaken.

1407
01:00:00.060 --> 01:00:07.980
So then I went forward to Goodbye Michael, same credit sequence, her wig is red.

1408
01:00:08.540 --> 01:00:09.160
What?

1409
01:00:09.440 --> 01:00:09.940
Yeah.

1410
01:00:10.180 --> 01:00:12.200
I took screenshots of both.

1411
01:00:12.500 --> 01:00:15.440
Look, here's the shot from Andy's play.

1412
01:00:16.480 --> 01:00:17.800
That's Goodbye Michael.

1413
01:00:17.800 --> 01:00:20.200
Oh my gosh, that is bizarre.

1414
01:00:20.820 --> 01:00:22.160
What is that about?

1415
01:00:22.700 --> 01:00:27.880
Yeah, they clearly went in and recolored the wig for this credit sequence in Goodbye Michael.

1416
01:00:28.160 --> 01:00:32.340
But they'd been playing it with a blonde one the whole time, the rest of the season.

1417
01:00:32.600 --> 01:00:33.880
There's got to be a reason.

1418
01:00:34.080 --> 01:00:35.240
You know who we're going to ask.

1419
01:00:35.300 --> 01:00:36.140
We're going to ask Randy.

1420
01:00:36.400 --> 01:00:38.800
So when we get to it, we'll have an answer.

1421
01:00:39.060 --> 01:00:42.160
Emily, thank you so much for pointing that out.

1422
01:00:42.260 --> 01:00:42.400
I know.

1423
01:00:42.400 --> 01:00:43.100
That was bonkers.

1424
01:00:43.280 --> 01:00:44.460
Fantastic catch, Emily.

1425
01:00:44.460 --> 01:00:49.660
Emily, in the kitchen, Todd Packer is sitting with a bunch of, well, they're like little

1426
01:00:49.660 --> 01:00:50.940
brown lunch bags.

1427
01:00:51.540 --> 01:00:53.620
And they list all these different organs.

1428
01:00:53.840 --> 01:00:56.000
And the last one is in his lap.

1429
01:00:56.200 --> 01:00:57.720
And it says trouser mouse.

1430
01:00:58.180 --> 01:00:58.500
Mm-hmm.

1431
01:00:59.020 --> 01:01:01.320
Danny says, I don't think that's going to go the way you hope it will.

1432
01:01:04.210 --> 01:01:08.070
Well, Jim's going to come into the kitchen and he is going to confront Danny.

1433
01:01:08.250 --> 01:01:09.910
He's going to say, hey, man, I'm just curious.

1434
01:01:09.910 --> 01:01:12.190
How come you never called my wife back for that date?

1435
01:01:12.890 --> 01:01:14.110
And Danny's like, really?

1436
01:01:14.450 --> 01:01:14.830
Mm-hmm.

1437
01:01:14.830 --> 01:01:15.590
Oh.

1438
01:01:16.470 --> 01:01:18.650
Packer's like, you're looking for someone to bang your wife?

1439
01:01:18.770 --> 01:01:20.830
I love that line so much.

1440
01:01:21.010 --> 01:01:22.190
It made me laugh out loud.

1441
01:01:22.970 --> 01:01:24.010
Danny says, you know what?

1442
01:01:24.230 --> 01:01:28.850
The truth is, I didn't call her back because all she talked about was you.

1443
01:01:29.150 --> 01:01:30.690
She was clearly in love with you.

1444
01:01:31.050 --> 01:01:32.130
Well, that's not true.

1445
01:01:32.390 --> 01:01:33.470
No, it's not.

1446
01:01:33.670 --> 01:01:38.410
There's a deleted scene where you see Jim walk over to Pam, whisper something in her

1447
01:01:38.410 --> 01:01:41.410
ear, and she looks at him and shakes her head like, nope, uh-uh.

1448
01:01:42.490 --> 01:01:46.630
And then the next scene is them confronting him outside of the men's room.

1449
01:01:47.010 --> 01:01:47.390
Yeah.

1450
01:01:47.730 --> 01:01:51.590
And they demand to know the real reason why he never called her.

1451
01:01:51.750 --> 01:01:54.990
Because if he doesn't tell her, it's just going to keep gnawing at her like,

1452
01:01:55.070 --> 01:01:56.230
nah, nah, nah, nah, nah, nah, nah.

1453
01:01:56.230 --> 01:01:59.250
I thought you were so fantastic in this scene again.

1454
01:01:59.250 --> 01:02:03.210
I looked at the shooting draft to see if there was any stage direction.

1455
01:02:03.510 --> 01:02:04.850
This was just all you.

1456
01:02:05.270 --> 01:02:09.950
The only thing they spelled out for you was the, excuse me.

1457
01:02:09.950 --> 01:02:12.790
Yes, it was all scripted.

1458
01:02:13.010 --> 01:02:15.610
One part that I added was that, ah, ah, ah, ah.

1459
01:02:15.790 --> 01:02:17.110
Yes, that was so great.

1460
01:02:17.370 --> 01:02:20.830
All it says in the shooting draft is that you awkwardly exit.

1461
01:02:20.830 --> 01:02:23.170
And how you chose to do that was all you.

1462
01:02:23.450 --> 01:02:31.070
I showed the scene to Lee because I said to him, this might be one of the most me performances

1463
01:02:31.070 --> 01:02:32.590
I've ever given.

1464
01:02:33.230 --> 01:02:34.990
I am a little dorky.

1465
01:02:34.990 --> 01:02:41.650
And I feel like the writers were on to something about me, Jenna, because I do all of these

1466
01:02:41.650 --> 01:02:43.090
things in my life.

1467
01:02:43.290 --> 01:02:45.130
And you also remember stuff.

1468
01:02:45.270 --> 01:02:47.050
So you would be the one like, nope, nope, it was two.

1469
01:02:47.170 --> 01:02:47.650
We had a third.

1470
01:02:47.810 --> 01:02:48.470
You didn't call.

1471
01:02:48.830 --> 01:02:50.010
That's how it went down.

1472
01:02:50.390 --> 01:02:50.910
Yeah.

1473
01:02:51.110 --> 01:02:56.550
They also really made all of this even more awkward by the fact that I am in a full,

1474
01:02:57.230 --> 01:02:58.990
elaborate, wigged costume.

1475
01:02:58.990 --> 01:03:04.570
And I'm talking to these two handsome men just dressed in normal clothes.

1476
01:03:04.570 --> 01:03:08.230
It really even further highlights Pam's dorkiness.

1477
01:03:08.470 --> 01:03:09.190
And I love it.

1478
01:03:09.410 --> 01:03:12.230
And your little flat ponytail kept flopping around.

1479
01:03:12.570 --> 01:03:14.670
I loved doing this scene.

1480
01:03:14.690 --> 01:03:16.450
And I really am so proud of it.

1481
01:03:17.050 --> 01:03:19.570
We had a fan question from Ashley W.

1482
01:03:19.810 --> 01:03:21.690
in Suffolk, Virginia, who said,

1483
01:03:21.830 --> 01:03:25.070
why does Danny Cordray disappear after this episode?

1484
01:03:25.190 --> 01:03:26.910
I loved the character.

1485
01:03:27.370 --> 01:03:30.370
And Timothy Oliphant isn't too shabby to look at either.

1486
01:03:30.930 --> 01:03:37.370
I'll tell you, he is mentioned again in Michael's last dundies when Michael gives him the hottest

1487
01:03:37.370 --> 01:03:38.630
in the office award.

1488
01:03:39.150 --> 01:03:42.770
And there was a little bit where Michael tries to bring Danny up via satellite,

1489
01:03:42.770 --> 01:03:44.150
and it got cut out.

1490
01:03:44.290 --> 01:03:45.370
It's in the deleted scenes.

1491
01:03:45.930 --> 01:03:47.850
You know, the story is that Danny's on the road.

1492
01:03:47.990 --> 01:03:50.490
It's how we see Todd Packer so infrequently.

1493
01:03:51.130 --> 01:03:54.970
But this storyline did kind of get unresolved.

1494
01:03:55.030 --> 01:03:59.790
I agree, Ashley, because that scene was cut from Michael's last dundies.

1495
01:03:59.990 --> 01:04:03.470
We assume that after Michael leaves, Danny is let go.

1496
01:04:03.670 --> 01:04:06.510
He was a hire we didn't really need.

1497
01:04:06.510 --> 01:04:08.510
We already had our traveling salesman.

1498
01:04:09.010 --> 01:04:13.350
But anyway, that you would have had at least a little nugget of information on him.

1499
01:04:13.850 --> 01:04:17.770
Well, we're about to have a sit down with Gabe, Daryl, and Michael to resolve all of this

1500
01:04:17.770 --> 01:04:22.070
issue of who brings what information to what department, right?

1501
01:04:22.750 --> 01:04:23.110
Yeah.

1502
01:04:23.450 --> 01:04:26.970
Gabe is going to tell Daryl that Daryl needs to get Michael's approval before coming to

1503
01:04:26.970 --> 01:04:27.550
him with anything.

1504
01:04:27.670 --> 01:04:28.530
And Daryl says, well, you know what?

1505
01:04:28.550 --> 01:04:30.030
You're going to miss out on some good ideas.

1506
01:04:30.410 --> 01:04:32.710
And then Gabe goes, well, then my door is always opened.

1507
01:04:33.050 --> 01:04:36.870
And this leads to a back and forth where Michael's like, after everything I've done for

1508
01:04:36.870 --> 01:04:37.090
you.

1509
01:04:37.090 --> 01:04:43.250
And Daryl looks at Michael and says, listen, Ed Truck hired me, Joe promoted me, Gabe listened

1510
01:04:43.250 --> 01:04:43.690
to me.

1511
01:04:43.890 --> 01:04:45.950
All you've ever done is say no to me.

1512
01:04:46.070 --> 01:04:47.150
I have ambition.

1513
01:04:47.510 --> 01:04:52.350
This is part of Daryl's storyline of where his ambition is going to take him.

1514
01:04:52.450 --> 01:04:56.690
And he's really starting to feel it, like he has good ideas, and they're changing the

1515
01:04:56.690 --> 01:04:57.850
way the company works.

1516
01:04:58.170 --> 01:05:03.790
And he's going to have a scene with Andy where he initially says, sometimes I think things

1517
01:05:03.790 --> 01:05:04.950
were better down in the warehouse.

1518
01:05:04.950 --> 01:05:09.450
And then Andy goes on this very sort of elaborate metaphor.

1519
01:05:09.810 --> 01:05:10.850
Using acapella.

1520
01:05:11.110 --> 01:05:11.530
Yes.

1521
01:05:11.810 --> 01:05:16.910
And at the end of this scene, Daryl says he does have big plans.

1522
01:05:17.150 --> 01:05:17.410
Yeah.

1523
01:05:17.690 --> 01:05:18.530
And big ambitions.

1524
01:05:18.530 --> 01:05:22.590
And we're going to see that storyline now play out through the rest of the series.

1525
01:05:23.170 --> 01:05:23.370
Yeah.

1526
01:05:23.930 --> 01:05:25.490
And Michael and Daryl make up.

1527
01:05:25.630 --> 01:05:29.750
They both decide if they ever disagree with Gabe, they're going to go straight to Joe.

1528
01:05:29.930 --> 01:05:31.190
And they shake hands on it.

1529
01:05:31.550 --> 01:05:32.730
Michael says, you know what?

1530
01:05:32.830 --> 01:05:33.530
Friends fight.

1531
01:05:34.390 --> 01:05:34.830
Mm-hmm.

1532
01:05:35.550 --> 01:05:38.390
Well, I like that Daryl got to call Michael out in this episode.

1533
01:05:38.550 --> 01:05:39.250
He deserved it.

1534
01:05:40.170 --> 01:05:42.150
Jim is going to have a very sweet talking head.

1535
01:05:42.930 --> 01:05:45.790
He's going to say, to be honest, I can't believe he didn't call her back.

1536
01:05:45.910 --> 01:05:47.710
Who doesn't call a dork like that back?

1537
01:05:48.290 --> 01:05:55.830
And now Jim is going to arrive dressed in the Popeye costume with Cece as Sweet Pea, her hero.

1538
01:05:56.790 --> 01:06:00.030
How cute did they look all dressed up?

1539
01:06:00.030 --> 01:06:02.170
I mean, I'm sorry.

1540
01:06:02.170 --> 01:06:02.350
I mean, I'm sorry.

1541
01:06:02.850 --> 01:06:05.370
It was so freaking adorable.

1542
01:06:05.790 --> 01:06:12.290
Did every woman's heart leap out of her chest when he walked in the door as Popeye carrying Sweet Pea or what?

1543
01:06:12.290 --> 01:06:13.330
So cute.

1544
01:06:13.570 --> 01:06:14.690
So cute.

1545
01:06:14.690 --> 01:06:21.250
The day we filmed that, I took a picture of John in the Popeye costume and holding the sweet little baby.

1546
01:06:21.530 --> 01:06:22.910
I still have the picture.

1547
01:06:23.150 --> 01:06:23.890
It's so cute.

1548
01:06:24.450 --> 01:06:26.350
Well, John is very much like Steve.

1549
01:06:26.630 --> 01:06:28.770
They both just love kids so much.

1550
01:06:28.950 --> 01:06:33.090
And John and I would just dote on those little babies all the time.

1551
01:06:33.230 --> 01:06:33.570
I know.

1552
01:06:33.570 --> 01:06:35.370
I loved having those girls on set.

1553
01:06:36.950 --> 01:06:40.590
We are now going to reveal who won the coupon book.

1554
01:06:40.830 --> 01:06:45.830
We get to see some people flash up their cards, kind of like Survivor style, who they wrote down.

1555
01:06:46.690 --> 01:06:48.010
Kelly voted for Oscar.

1556
01:06:48.250 --> 01:06:49.510
Ryan voted for Oscar.

1557
01:06:49.850 --> 01:06:51.170
Creed voted for Oscar.

1558
01:06:51.790 --> 01:06:52.790
Oscar won.

1559
01:06:53.010 --> 01:06:53.410
Yeah.

1560
01:06:53.830 --> 01:06:55.970
There was a scene that would have come after this.

1561
01:06:56.130 --> 01:06:57.310
It's in Deleted Scenes.

1562
01:06:57.750 --> 01:07:02.790
Creed, Meredith, Ryan, Kelly, and Angela have gathered around Oscar as he reads from the coupon book.

1563
01:07:02.790 --> 01:07:04.170
Oh, I love this.

1564
01:07:04.410 --> 01:07:06.730
I feel like they gave Oscar a lot of alts for this.

1565
01:07:06.890 --> 01:07:10.690
Here are a few that were in the script as well as deleted scenes.

1566
01:07:11.190 --> 01:07:12.210
Oscar says,

1567
01:07:12.530 --> 01:07:16.650
Who wants $30 off any full fare ticket on a flight to Chicago?

1568
01:07:17.090 --> 01:07:18.290
Blackout dates apply.

1569
01:07:19.930 --> 01:07:23.190
Who wants a free power boost at Body Shake's Boba Bar?

1570
01:07:23.950 --> 01:07:29.330
Who wants a 100 megabyte MP3 player special bonus does not play iTunes?

1571
01:07:29.910 --> 01:07:32.210
Who wants a free estimate on carpet cleaning?

1572
01:07:32.950 --> 01:07:33.810
Oh, look.

1573
01:07:33.950 --> 01:07:35.870
5% off your Dunder Mifflin order.

1574
01:07:36.130 --> 01:07:37.890
Ask for Stan the Man.

1575
01:07:38.090 --> 01:07:42.990
And then the camera reveals a smiling photo of Stanley from 20 years ago.

1576
01:07:43.450 --> 01:07:44.610
I have a question.

1577
01:07:44.610 --> 01:07:46.890
How are people reacting in the scene?

1578
01:07:46.990 --> 01:07:47.970
Are they getting it?

1579
01:07:48.050 --> 01:07:51.130
Are they, like, finally getting that maybe the coupon book wasn't great?

1580
01:07:51.210 --> 01:07:53.390
Or are they still wishing they had the coupon book?

1581
01:07:53.610 --> 01:07:54.010
No.

1582
01:07:54.110 --> 01:07:54.830
With each one, they're like,

1583
01:07:54.930 --> 01:07:55.650
Ah, pass.

1584
01:07:55.810 --> 01:07:55.890
Ah.

1585
01:07:55.890 --> 01:07:59.150
And then Kelly's like, Oscar, get to the good stuff.

1586
01:07:59.510 --> 01:08:02.050
And then that's when he gets to Stan the Man.

1587
01:08:02.530 --> 01:08:03.350
That's great.

1588
01:08:04.050 --> 01:08:07.770
Oh, well, guys, that was Costume ConteSt.

1589
